<figure id="attachment_74136" aria-describedby="caption-attachment-74136" style="width: 800px" class="wp-caption alignnone"><img decoding="async" src="https://www.futilitycloset.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/2026-09-03-synopsis-1.png" alt="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Maze-05_Barcelona_Parc_del_Laberint_(system_of_paths_and_nodes).PNG" width="800" height="600" class="size-full wp-image-74136" srcset="https://www.futilitycloset.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/2026-09-03-synopsis-1.png 800w, https://www.futilitycloset.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/2026-09-03-synopsis-1-600x450.png 600w, https://www.futilitycloset.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/2026-09-03-synopsis-1-300x225.png 300w" sizes="(max-width: 800px) 100vw, 800px" /><figcaption id="caption-attachment-74136" class="wp-caption-text">Image: <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Maze-05_Barcelona_Parc_del_Laberint_(system_of_paths_and_nodes).PNG">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure>
<p>Mazes are designed to be tortuous, so even a published solution can be hard to follow. A &#8220;straight-line diagram&#8221; dispenses with the windings and converts the essential puzzle in a simple map that&#8217;s easy to interpret:</p>
<figure id="attachment_74137" aria-describedby="caption-attachment-74137" style="width: 800px" class="wp-caption alignnone"><img decoding="async" src="https://www.futilitycloset.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/2026-09-03-synopsis-2.png" alt="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Maze-06_Barcelona_Parc_del_Laberint_(straight_line_diagram).PNG" width="800" height="400" class="size-full wp-image-74137" srcset="https://www.futilitycloset.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/2026-09-03-synopsis-2.png 800w, https://www.futilitycloset.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/2026-09-03-synopsis-2-600x300.png 600w, https://www.futilitycloset.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/2026-09-03-synopsis-2-300x150.png 300w" sizes="(max-width: 800px) 100vw, 800px" /><figcaption id="caption-attachment-74137" class="wp-caption-text">Image: <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Maze-06_Barcelona_Parc_del_Laberint_(straight_line_diagram).PNG">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure>
<p>This example summarizes the hedge maze in Barcelona&#8217;s Parc del Laberint d&#8217;Horta.</p>
<p>The same can be done with any meandering route &#8212; many subways have adopted stylized maps that dispense with geography and focus on the order of stops, the most important detail for most commuters.</p>
